## Content specs · 12 missing documents

Builder generates Romanian text following the style of the 4 existing §23.3 docs (same voice, same level of detail). Each doc must include at least one missing field, risk flag, or unresolved item — the AI is meant to surface these.

```
SUPPLIER INVOICES (4)

invoice_mobila_artisan_2026_0187.pdf
  supplier   Mobila Artisan SRL · CUI RO00000003 · IBAN RO00BANK0000000000000003
  items      custom shelving · 4 modules @ 720 RON/buc + montaj 280 RON
  total      ~3140 RON · TVA included
  due        21.05.2026
  twist      delivery confirmed verbally but no signed acceptance protocol attached
  urgency    Medium

invoice_printstudio_2026_0098.pdf
  supplier   PrintStudio Media SRL · CUI RO00000004
  items      promotional materials (catalogs, business cards) · ~850 RON total
  due        already paid 02.05.2026 (per accountant email this needs payment confirmation forwarding)
  twist      payment was made but proof not yet sent to accountant
  urgency    Medium

invoice_curier_rapid_2026_1142.pdf
  supplier   Curier Rapid Express SRL · CUI RO00000005
  items      delivery services aprilie 2026 · ~440 RON
  due        15.05.2026
  twist      one delivery (poz 3) is disputed — recipient claims package was incomplete
  urgency    Low

invoice_softcloud_2026_0520.pdf
  supplier   SoftCloud Solutions SRL · CUI RO00000006
  items      monthly subscription · cloud hosting + backup · 220 RON/lună
  due        18.05.2026
  twist      the accountant flagged this — no record of who approved the subscription
             (links back to email_accountant_missing_docs_april.txt point #4)
  urgency    High

CLIENT EMAILS (2)

email_client_showroom_pitesti.txt
  sender     existing client tied to contract_client_showroom_renovation
  topic      asks for status update on renovation phase 1 milestones
  twist      mentions a date that does not match the contract's milestone schedule
  urgency    Medium

email_client_intarziere_livrare.txt
  sender     a different client
  topic      complaint about a 5-day delay on a custom delivery
  twist      polite but firm · asks for compensation or partial discount
  urgency    High

SUPPLIER OFFERS (2)

offer_lumina_led_panels.txt
  from       Lumina Design SRL (existing supplier)
  proposes   new generation LED panels at a 12% discount if order placed before 31.05.2026
  twist      discount is contingent on minimum 30-unit order
  urgency    Low

offer_mobila_custom_shelves.txt
  from       Mobila Artisan SRL (existing supplier)
  proposes   custom shelving for a hypothetical second showroom · sample pricing
  twist      includes lead time of 6 weeks · doesn't match Atelier Nova's typical project timing
  urgency    Low

CONTRACT (1)

contract_client_showroom_renovation.txt
  parties    Atelier Nova SRL · client (synthetic SRL name)
  scope      complete renovation of a 220 sqm showroom in Pitești · 3 milestone phases
  payment    40% advance · 40% mid-project · 20% on acceptance
  duration   start 15.04.2026 · end target 30.06.2026
  penalties  0.1% per day for delays past 30.06.2026
  twist      penalty clause is stricter than the supplier-side Lumina contract — flag this for review
  urgency    Medium

INTERNAL (3)

policy_hr_remote_work.txt
  scope      remote work policy · who is eligible · approval process · required tools
  notes      mentions a 2-day-per-week max · no public version yet
  urgency    Low

procedure_client_project_intake.txt
  scope      step-by-step procedure for taking on a new client project
  steps      consultation → site visit → offer → contract → kickoff
  twist      step 4 references a "standard contract template" that does not yet exist as a document
  urgency    Low

price_list_services_2026.txt
  scope      service price list 2026 · consultation · design · project management · custom items
  notes      includes a footnote that prices are subject to revision after Q2 2026
  urgency    Low
```

For each doc, builder produces:
- `rawContent` (Romanian, plausible business prose)
- `summary` (English, 1-2 sentences, mentions the twist/missing item)
- `suggestedAction` (English, practical next step)
- `fields[]`, `missingFields[]`, `riskFlags[]` per the `InboxDoc` shape from slice-1
- `audit[]` with at least one initial AI-analyzed event

---

## Mock RAG strategy (resolved)

```
canned Q&A      8 questions from project_control_pack §23.3 "Example Ask My Company Questions"
                each → fixed answer text + cited source filenames from the 16-doc set
                question 5 ("Draft a reply to the apartment client") → answer routes user to /app/inbox
                with the apartament card and explains the Draft Reply panel exists there

fallback        any question not matched by exact-or-close keyword set:
                "Information not found in your documents."
                + small hint listing the 8 example questions

honest mode     no fake confidence · no fabricated sources · "not found" is a feature not a bug
                this is the same shape the real RAG will use in slice-3
```

---

## Draft Reply strategy (resolved)

```
who           only docs with type === 'Client Request'  (3 total: existing apartament + 2 new)
where         new collapsible panel inside the existing /app/inbox doc detail view
content       pre-canned Romanian draft per client doc · written by builder
states        Suggested → Approved (button click) → audit event logged
no Send       no Send button visible · only Approve / Edit-locally / Discard
              Edit-locally lets user modify text in-page · changes do not persist (no backend)
              Discard removes the draft · audit event logged
```

---

## Builder prompt

Copy this into a fresh IDE session (Sonnet) at `/home/innerpixel/dev/sme-companion`:

```text
Read CLAUDE.md, ops/project.state.hybrid, ops/rules.constraints.hybrid, and ops/slice-2.demo-data.hybrid.

You are the builder for slice-2. Coordinator (opus) has defined scope and resolved the open edges; you execute.

Reference docs are in codocz/ (e.g., codocz/romanian_sme_ai_companion_project_control_pack.md §23.3).

Tasks (commit in checkpoints — 1 commit after each major task):

1. Author the 12 missing demo documents per slice-2 §Content specs. For each:
   - Generate plausible Romanian rawContent following the voice/length of the 4 existing §23.3 docs.
   - Build the InboxDoc object (shape from src/lib/data/inbox.ts) with English summary/action and Romanian rawContent.
   - Ensure the "twist" from the spec surfaces in missingFields or riskFlags or summary.
   - Append all 12 to INBOX_DOCS in src/lib/data/inbox.ts. You may group them with comment headers by type (// === Supplier Invoices === etc).
   Commit: "slice-2(content): 12 synthetic demo documents complete"

2. Build src/lib/data/qa.ts with canned Q&A pairs per slice-2 §Mock RAG strategy. Export a typed QA_PAIRS array and a matchQuestion(input: string): QAResult function (returns matched answer + cited filenames, or null for fallback).
   Commit: "slice-2(qa): canned Ask My Company question/answer pairs"

3. Build /app/ask route — chat-style UI. Static layout: input box at bottom, message list above. On submit: matchQuestion → render answer with cited source pills (clickable to /app/inbox?focus=<id>) OR render fallback "Information not found" + hint. No streaming animation needed.
   Update /app/+layout.svelte sidebar: add "Ask My Company" entry between Inbox and any future entries.
   Commit: "slice-2(ask): /app/ask Ask My Company mock with canned answers"

4. Build src/lib/data/replies.ts with pre-canned Romanian Draft Reply content for the 3 client_request docs. Type: { docId: string; subject: string; body: string }[].

5. Add Draft Reply panel to /app/inbox doc detail view (collapsible, only renders when type === 'Client Request'). Show subject + body in Romanian, three actions: Approve · Edit-locally · Discard. Approve sets a reactive approval state and appends an audit event. Edit-locally swaps to a textarea (changes don't persist). Discard hides the panel and logs an audit event. No Send button anywhere — verify before commit.
   Commit: "slice-2(reply): Draft Reply panel for client requests"

6. Verify acceptance criteria from slice-2 §Acceptance manually. Note any deviations.

7. When done:
   - npm run check → must pass clean (or document the noise)
   - npm run build → must succeed
   - append ONE PATCHLOG line to ops/slice-2.demo-data.hybrid (timestamp · model · summary)
   - update STATE in slice-2 frontmatter from "forming" to "stable"
   - append ONE PATCHLOG line to ops/project.state.hybrid; update §Now (current → slice-3.backend) and §Slices (slice-2 → stable)
   - final commit: "slice-2: codon shipped · state→stable"

Constraints (anchored — do not violate):
- All content synthetic. Synthetic CUI/IBAN/names matching existing pattern (RO0000000N).
- Romanian for document rawContent, English for summary/action/UI.
- No Send button. Anywhere. Ever.
- Visual palette unchanged.
- Tone calm, no hype. Reference: codocz/romanian_sme_ai_companion_promotion_go_to_market_pack.md §4-§5.

Confirm the plan in 3 lines, then start with task 1. Stop and report back if scope drifts or you hit a blocker — append to slice-2 OPEN EDGES, commit what you have.
```

